# fraud-memory-agent environment configuration
# Copy to .env in this folder, demos/fraud-amazon-quick/, and fill in your
# values:
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# The file sits outside fraud-memory-agent/, so the AgentCore CLI never
# packages it into the Runtime code zip. The agent loads it for local runs,
# and `agent.sh` loads it for deploys. Existing environment variables are
# never overridden. The deployed Runtime does not read this file.

# =============================================================================
# NAMS memory (required)
# =============================================================================
# Create an API key at https://memory.neo4jlabs.com. Local runs read it from
# here. `agent.sh deploy` stores it in AgentCore Identity as the nams-api-key
# credential, and the Runtime reads it from there.
MEMORY_API_KEY=nams_your-api-key

# Optional for a private or staging NAMS deployment.
#MEMORY_ENDPOINT=https://memory.neo4jlabs.com/v1
#MEMORY_WORKSPACE_ID=your-workspace-id

# Optional. Give the agent NAMS memory tools it can call on its own (search
# context, entity provenance, feedback, read-only Cypher). Off by default
# because these tools search the whole NAMS workspace, not only the current
# user's memory. The automatic recall of a user's earlier turns is always on
# and stays limited to that user.
#MEMORY_TOOLS=true

# The agent reaches Neo4j through MCP, so it needs no NEO4J_* values. The
# graph loader keeps its own settings in
# demos/fraud-amazon-quick/graph-loader/.env.

# =============================================================================
# Model + region (optional; defaults shown)
# =============================================================================
# AWS credentials come from the standard chain: env vars, ~/.aws, or an
# instance role.

#MODEL_ID=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
#AWS_REGION=us-west-2
